export anchor ArcticExpeditionStyle:
    number: 423
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Arctic expedition
    idea: The trip kept as a polar expedition log, a dark graph paper logbook with an orange margin line where each leg is a dated entry, beside a contoured route sheet with camp triangles, a weather observation table, a taped kit list and a provisions fund drawn as ration blocks.
    base: dark
    palette:
        polarNight: #0a1118, the page and the style sheet
        logPage: #101b25, the logbook and note cards
        grid: #18283a, graph paper lines on the logbook
        line: #24394c, card edges and dashed table rules
        ink: #e6f1f8, text
        muted: #9fb5c6, labels, captions and flight entries
        ice: #a8dcff, headings, the route, camps, the booked entry rule and the primary button
        onIce: #06202f, text on ice
        frost: #d6f0ff, the focus ring
        signal: #ff9a5c, the margin line, Not booked and To do
        secured: #8fe3c0, Booked and Done
    type:
        Notes in system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto at 15px. Log heads, labels and
        stamps in ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo at 12px bold caps
        tracked 0.12 to 0.16em in ice. The log title 44px at 700, entry
        titles 20px at 700, the fund figure 32px tabular.
    layout:
        A thin header band in monospace caps with a star and BRIGHTWORK
        TRIPS in ice on the left and Expedition log No. 01 on the right.
        Below, two columns. The left is the logbook, a dark page ruled as
        24px graph paper with an orange margin line near its left edge. It
        opens with Field notes for, Japan in April in bold, and Leader Mara
        Okafor, Party 2 with one guest and Window 1 to 14 April 2027. Log
        entries follows, six boxed entries right of the margin, each with a
        diamond bullet on the margin, a monospace head such as Day 1 or Days
        6 to 10 with the date, a title, a note and a status stamp. Booked
        entries have a solid ice left rule and solid diamond, unbooked a
        dashed orange rule and hollow diamond, flights grey. Two buttons
        follow. The right column holds a route sheet tilted slightly with a
        shadow, contour lines, a grid, a north arrow and a dashed ice route
        between three camp triangles for Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka. Then three
        taped note cards. Conditions observed is a table of Station Tokyo,
        Period Early April, Highs around 17 degrees and a blossom note. Kit
        list shows the four checks. Provisions fund shows 3,200 euro of
        5,000 laid in over five ration blocks of 1,000, three full, one a
        fifth full, one dashed empty. Below 960px the columns stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit on a 24px graph grid. 14px between log entries, 20px between note cards and 28px between columns.
    density: Medium. Six entries in the log and four note cards beside it.
    corners: Nearly square at 2px. The route sheet tilts by 0.6 degrees and tape strips by 3.
    borders: 1px slate edges and a 3px left rule on every entry, solid ice when booked and dashed signal orange when not. Dashed rules in tables.
    shadows: Only under the tilted route sheet. Pale tape strips hold the cards.
    icons:
        Field marks. Booked is a solid flag, Not booked a dashed empty
        square and Flight a plane. Entry bullets are diamonds, hollow when
        unbooked. Camps are triangles. Done is a ticked box and To do an
        empty box.
    focus: A 2px frost outline offset 2px with a soft ice halo.
    tone: Plain expedition speech such as Log entries, Conditions observed, Kit list and Provisions fund.
